+#### 9.6 Reopening the Institution's Systems
+
+*In plain terms: when an institution is found to have governed badly in a way that matters, each of its systems is reopened for a fresh look as soon as notice is given, unless that system's own review is already under way. That is a fresh look and not a verdict. Each system keeps its status until its own review decides.*
+
+When an Institution has a **governance violation**, review of each System it operates, stewards, or materially controls reopens. The name does not mean a violation for standing; it names the reopening grounds below. A governance violation is any one of these, and only a material one reopens (see *Material only* below):
+
+- **A determination that its governance failed:** a determination that the Institution's own governance failed on one of these items of [§3 Whole-Institution Certification Evaluation](#3-whole-institution-certification-evaluation): the Institutional Charter against practice (item 1), portfolio and aggregate effect (item 2), accountable authority (item 3), rewards and incentives (item 4), the Role Map and custody (item 5), office-holder standing and authenticity (item 7), or the Institution's own institutional duties (item 8). It also covers a defect in the Institution's own conduct under an evaluation in [§4 Evaluations Where Implicated](#4-evaluations-where-implicated) or [§5 Rights-Floor and Domain Evaluations](#5-rights-floor-and-domain-evaluations), or under the systemic-risk or data types and handling parts of Chapter Nine Part A §3 Whole-System Certification Evaluation that apply to the Institution. It may be made in the Institution's certification pass, in a recertification or reopened review, or in a forum case. Where it is made in a certification evaluation it counts even if the result is only that the Institution is not yet aligned, which is not a violation for standing ([Chapter Nine Part C §11.2 Every certification outcome](core_09.010_system_alignment_certification_record_recertification.md#112-every-certification-outcome)).
+- **A denial or revocation of the Institution** on a denial or revocation ground that lies in the matters above, or in the conduct of its governing authority under [§7.4 Denial and revocation for an Institution](#74-denial-and-revocation-for-an-institution) (unwillingness, evidence shown to be false, fabricated, or concealed, a certification condition missed twice or materially violated, or a required proof step not done).
+- **An institutional cause:** a cause finding under rule 2 of [§9.5 Cascade from System certifications](#95-cascade-from-system-certifications) that places the cause of a cited System's misalignment in the Institution's own governance, incentives, resourcing, Institutional Charter, or portfolio. That System is already in review; every other System the Institution operates, stewards, or materially controls reopens.
