+
+- **First certification:**
+  - **Record:** it is due inside the window in [Chapter Ten §1.3 Window for the first certification](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#13-window-for-the-first-certification). With no System, there is one Institutional Certification Record on its own and no System Certification Record to cite ([Chapter Ten §1.1 Who is certified](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#11-who-is-certified)).
+  - **What evaluation must test:** the eight items of [Chapter Ten §3 Whole-Institution Certification Evaluation](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#3-whole-institution-certification-evaluation), simplified for Class L but none omitted, and an item with nothing to find is stated in a line. The core is the Institutional Charter against practice, the Charter Role Map (is the record seat outside the trust's own line of control?), the formation check statement (the currency of cited System certifications does not arise, as the trust runs no System), and item 8 (do the trust's member complaint and answer routes work in fact, and do they answer in time?).
+  - **Result:** provisional certification.
+- **Later, new authority:**
+  - **What changes:** the trust decides to run a hardship loan fund. Who gets a loan is a new kind of decision over members, material to them and not covered by its Institutional Charter.
+  - **What happens:** the trust gives notice of the Institutional Charter amendment. The screen finds no blocker. At Class L an automated clearance counts as the official response, the clearance is published with the challenge path open, and the trust starts the fund. A member who fears the fund's terms can challenge the clearance and ask for interim protection.
+- **What the record must show:** the class and its reasons, the eight items with the findings or the one-line statement for each, the notice and the date of clearance, and the challenge path.
+
+**One System: a clinic-scheduling company.** The company runs exactly one System that needs a System Charter, a triage scheduler. It has a single one-System evaluation and one record ([Chapter Ten §1.1 Who is certified](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#11-who-is-certified)).
+
+- **What evaluation finds:** the scheduler itself is sound, and the System side has no defect. But the company pays its appeals staff a bonus for fewer reversals, which in practice rewards turning appeals away. These are appeals of the staff's own decisions, not of the scheduler's, so [Chapter Nine Part A §3.1 Governance, Incentive, and Contestability Discipline](../core_09.000_system_alignment_certification_evaluation.md#31-governance-incentive-and-contestability-discipline) attributes the bonus to the company and not to the System. That is an institutional ground under item 4 (rewards and incentives) of [Chapter Ten §3 Whole-Institution Certification Evaluation](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#3-whole-institution-certification-evaluation). It is purely institutional: the bonus concerns the company's appeals staff and not the scheduler, so no fact in the System's own evaluation rests on it. The readiness check finds the company willing to change the bonus but not able, because a funder's contract fixes it for another eighteen months, and no narrower scope, support, or handover closes the gap in time ([Chapter Ten §7.3 Remediation readiness for an Institution](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#73-remediation-readiness-for-an-institution)). This is its first certification, so the institutional ground is a denial ground.
+- **Outcome:** under the *One System* bullet of [Chapter Ten §7.4 Denial and revocation for an Institution](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#74-denial-and-revocation-for-an-institution) (read with the one-System bullet of §7.3 Remediation readiness for an Institution) each outcome follows its own denial or revocation ground, and the record carries a status line for the System and one for the Institution.
+  - **The System:** it is not denied, because nothing in its own findings supports that.
+  - **Status lines:** the System's line reads provisional certification, and the Institution's line reads Not Certified.
+  - **The Institution:** the company is published as Not Certified, because the institutional ground supports that. It keeps operating and keeps running the scheduler.
+  - **Effects:** the notices under [Chapter Ten §7.5 Effects of denial and revocation for an Institution](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#75-effects-of-denial-and-revocation-for-an-institution) go out, including to the forums of the System; the status is adverse evidence when the System is next certified, and the company may not hold a seat in another body's certification until it changes the bonus and is recertified.
+- **What the record must show:** which denial ground supports which outcome, the cause finding (institutional), the interim protection and reliance limits, and the corrective work required.
+
+**Class A: a regional benefits platform with several Systems.** The Institution runs four Systems that decide who receives survival-essential benefits, which is why it is Class A, and each has its own System Certification Record. One Institutional Certification Record links to all four.
+
+- **The violation:** a forum case determines that one of its authorities, setting eligibility cut-offs, has no accountable office that can be named. That is a material failure of item 3 (accountable authority) of [Chapter Ten §3 Whole-Institution Certification Evaluation](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#3-whole-institution-certification-evaluation), and so a governance violation under [Chapter Ten §9.6 Reopening the Institution's Systems](../core_10.000_institutional_alignment_certification.md#96-reopening-the-institutions-systems).
+- **What happens:**
+  - **Notice:** the Institution's governing authority gives notice at once to the lead forum of each of the four Systems' certification passes. If it does not, the forum that made the determination gives it, to those lead forums and to the lead forum of the Institution's certification pass, inside the intake target of the Class A tier.
+  - **Reopened reviews:** each System's lead forum opens a reopened review with a new record linked to the last, on the tier windows. A System already inside a certification pass takes the determination into that pass, and no second pass is opened.
+  - **No verdict:** no System's status changes by the reopening, and no System is stopped. Each System's own certification pass decides what follows, on its own findings.
+- **What the record must show:** the determination, each System notified and the date of the notice, and, in each reopened review, the new record linked to the last.
+
+**Reading across the Institutions.** The same Chapter Ten text applies to each. What changes is the depth and the route: a Class L Institution with no System has a record of its own and a simplified evaluation, an Institution with one System has one evaluation whose two outcomes follow their own denial or revocation grounds, and an Institution with several Systems answers for them through links and through reopening, without any System's certification being decided in the Institution's. In none of them does a certification outcome decide whether the Institution may exist or operate, and the only wait is the one for new material authority.
+
